    "captions": [
      {
        "t": 0,
        "text": "Spring 1097. The princes' armies cross the Bosporus into Anatolia with Byzantine guides and supplies. Perhaps 50,000 to 60,000 people, including non-combatants, set out."
      },
      {
        "t": 0.2,
        "text": "May to June 1097. Nicaea, the Seljuk capital, is besieged for seven weeks and surrenders to the Byzantines."
      },
      {
        "t": 2.0,
        "text": "1 July 1097. Kilij Arslan ambushes the vanguard at Dorylaeum and is beaten off when the rest of the army arrives."
      },
      {
        "t": 2.2,
        "text": "July and August. The march across the dry Anatolian plateau in summer. Horses die in their hundreds and knights ride oxen or walk."
      },
      {
        "t": 4.3,
        "text": "September. At Heraclea Baldwin of Boulogne and Tancred turn south into Cilicia. The main army takes the longer road north through Caesarea, avoiding the Cilician Gates."
      },
      {
        "t": 5.65,
        "text": "21 October 1097. The army reaches Antioch, a huge walled city. The siege lasts more than seven months, through a winter of famine."
      },
      {
        "t": 9.65,
        "text": "February to March 1098. Baldwin, invited by the Armenians, becomes ruler of Edessa: the first crusader state."
      },
      {
        "t": 13.1,
        "text": "3 June 1098. Antioch is betrayed from within. Weeks later the crusaders march out and scatter Kerbogha's relief army."
      },
      {
        "t": 14.5,
        "text": "Summer and autumn 1098. Plague and quarrels between the princes hold the army at Antioch for five months. Bohemond keeps the city."
      },
      {
        "t": 19.4,
        "text": "December 1098. Ma'arrat al-Numan is stormed and its people killed. The rank and file force their leaders to move on."
      },
      {
        "t": 21.45,
        "text": "February to May 1099. Raymond of Toulouse besieges Arqa for three months, hoping to win a lordship, and fails."
      },
      {
        "t": 24.5,
        "text": "May 1099. The army marches fast down the coast. The emirs of Tripoli, Beirut and other towns pay them to pass by."
      },
      {
        "t": 25.2,
        "text": "7 June 1099. About 13,000 crusaders reach Jerusalem, held by a Fatimid garrison. On 15 July they take it."
      }
    ]
  },
